          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On April 02, 2009, around 11:10 PM, a witness observed in a cloudy sky a white phenomenon with a reddish glow, in the shape of a pinhead. This phenomenon moved very quickly in a zigzag pattern from South to West, giving the impression of descending towards the Pyrenees. The lack of information (questionnaire or report) does not allow for an investigation or the consideration of hypotheses. In this case, the GEIPAN classifies this case as category C due to the lack of information.",
